  "notes": "Beat-led composition, stated first-hand: \"When I heard that beat, it was clear; 'This is what I'ma say'. Every bar.\" The research draws the consequence and it is this model's central parameter — \"because the writing is beat-first the vocal melody is derived from the loop's top line rather than imposed on it; melodic cells reuse the loop's pitch set almost exactly.\" So `melody.chordToneBias` is 0.8 and the interval mix is heavily stepwise (0.68/0.24/0.08) with `octaveJumpProb` down at 0.1 against the parent's 0.34: this is a narrow, loop-shaped line, not the parent's leaping topline. The counter reuses the same pitch set, which is why octave_echo carries it. ⚠ `modes` is authored because the research says the drums are \"bench-dependent rather than personal\" and names the two benches: Ronny J's distorted/clipped kit on one side, JetsonMade's bounce-forward kit on the other. A producer-dependent artist is honestly modelled as two moods, not as an average of two kits that no record sounds like. The saturation follows the bench — `bass808.distortion` \"heavy\" on the Ronny J mode (the research: \"heavily saturated on the Ronny J material\") against \"light\" on the JetsonMade side, where the kick syncopation carries the bounce instead. ⚠ `confidence` is \"low\" because the research rates it medium-low. Documented: the Gold certification, and the compositional method quoted first-hand. INFERRED, and the research says so plainly — \"harmony, drums and 808 are inferred from the producers he used rather than sourced directly\": the BPM range, all drum placement, the 808 line (`slideProb` 0.4 with `anticipationProb` 0.34 for \"occasional slide into the downbeat\"), and every chord numeral. The i-VI / i-VII families are the inferred parameter. ⚠ `arrangement` is where the research is concrete: \"2-bar loop repeated with vocal-layer additions as the only development, sub-3:00 runtimes, abrupt endings\" — hence `switchUpProb` 0.06, a 2-bar outro, and one structure that simply stops on a hook.",
